# Implementation ↔ tests

- Changing behavior **implies** updating or adding tests that already cover that surface — green CI alone is not enough; assertions must match the **new** contract. Força / anti-padrões do caso → `test-quality-rails.mdc`.
- **Before finish:** locate counterpart tests (`test/models/x_test.rb` ↔ `app/models/x.rb`, request/system tests for routes / flows touched — naming varies by project; search by class, path, route).
- **Tela / action HTTP:** ao criar ou alterar controller, view ou rota de uma tela (HTML ou API), verificar se existe teste de integração/request (`test/integration/`, `test/requests/`) para aquela superfície. Se não existir, **criar**. O teste garante renderização/resposta e o status HTTP correto (`200`, `201`, `404`, `409`, `422`, …). Escopo **limitado** — não revalidar o negócio; detalhes → unitários. Como escrever → `writting-tests-rails.mdc`.
- **Contract drift:** renamed API, new branches, defaults, validations, HTTP status, side effects → change setup + assertions in those tests. Weakening tests to green is forbidden unless product explicitly drops the behavior (then delete/replace with documented intent).
- **No orphan RED:** do not treat work complete while tests for touched code still encode old behavior — except intentional TDD RED called out in workflow.
- **Run scope:** after edits, run tests tied to changed files (single file / line filter) — not only unrelated suite green.
- **New public behavior:** add or extend tests in the correct layer; updating one old assertion is insufficient when nothing covered the path before.
